  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indigenous People Participatory Video Training Pilot Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIMI Tefe and Hutakara are both key partners in the Indigeonous Support Programme. In order to support these indigenous peoples organisations fulfil their advocacy aims, CAFOD has proposed a pilot participatory video &apos;training for trainers&apos; workshop with the partner staff, which will involve working within two indigenous communities. The indigenous communities will be trained in how to use video as a tool to advocate for change to public policy, increase public awareness of the issues faced by indigenous people and show national and international audiences the sustainability of indigenous peoples&apos; livelihoods. The training will enable the partner staff to go on to train other indigenous communities in using participatory video as an advocacy tool. If successful this training may be rolled out to other partners in the indigenous support programme. This is a joint ID and CCS project which has come about as a result of a recent successful participatory video &apos;training for trainers&apos; project in Sierra Leone which produced significant learning that CAFOD is keen to utilize and build upon.</narrative>
  </description>
